1
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:17,520
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,900
onto the head of the carpenter
I was putting in a chokehold.

4
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:39,120
They laughed, saying I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I've left my spirit somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,180
pachinko, savings, even yawns,
aren't used in an emergency.

7
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:53,160
The town somehow feels strangely kind.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointy-hat water fountain,

9
00:01:01,780 --> 00:01:07,440
grand heavens, the sun sets.

10
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too,
it'll end just like this, won't it?

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,120
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness lost once again.

12
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:24,500
Because I'm a fool who finally realized it.

13
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:30,980
Bonus on top, pure profit.

14
00:01:51,660 --> 00:01:53,060
Yes! A hit!

15
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:54,500
Right, let's go to the next one!

16
00:01:55,020 --> 00:01:55,380
Yes!

17
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:58,218
Today's kids,

18
00:01:58,268 --> 00:02:01,200
do they have no interest
at all in a ghost contest?

19
00:02:01,340 --> 00:02:02,701
Well, that's true.

20
00:02:02,751 --> 00:02:06,561
Kids who are totally used to
the amazing SFX in recent movies

21
00:02:06,611 --> 00:02:10,600
will just laugh if you mention a
one-eyed kid or a faceless ghost.

22
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:13,780
What's this SF thing you're talking about?

23
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:16,580
Special effects, you know.
There's some amazing stuff out there.

24
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:20,400
Hey, don't spit your seeds over here,
Ryo-san.

25
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:27,800
When we were kids, we really looked forward to
ghost contests and test-of-courage events, you know.

26
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:32,620
Is this traditional shopping
street event going to disappear too?

27
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:34,320
It feels kind of lonely.

28
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:39,160
In short, we just need some kind of
setup that will make today's kids happy.

29
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:40,800
Do you already have an idea?

30
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:43,360
Well, leave it to me,
and nothing is impossible.

31
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:48,520
How about this: give me 10% of the stall sales at
the shopping street and let me handle everything.

32
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:49,400
You idiot!

33
00:02:52,460 --> 00:02:55,740
Do you charge the citizens

34
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:57,160
for every little favor?

35
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,320
You blockhead!

36
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:01,580
Chief, why are you helping out?

37
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:03,420
It's for training an unruly subordinate.

38
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:05,160
I just bought it at
the sporting goods store.

39
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:10,560
Providing free service to the citizens

40
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:13,940
is the duty of us police.

41
00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:16,700
Understand, Ryotsu?

42
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:18,080
Understood.

43
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:18,620
Yes.

44
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:24,800
Damn, this heat is murder, and working for
nothing on a day like this is a real pain.

45
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:28,400
Besides, I doubt modern kids would
be impressed by some one-eyed yokai.

46
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:32,020
Don't worry, leave it to me.
I'm confident about my makeup skills.

47
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:36,000
These are the latest special effects makeup materials,
imported straight from Hollywood.

48
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:38,240
They'll turn out so
realistic it'll blow your mind.

49
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:40,020
Alright, let's get started.

50
00:03:40,020 --> 00:03:41,580
Ugh, do whatever you want with me.

51
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:44,020
What I need you to prepare is

52
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:48,560
a bit of plaster, silicone, and foam latex.

53
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:50,120
Then let's get to work.

54
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:53,660
First, we'll apply silicone
to your face and take a mold.

55
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:57,240
Next, make a plaster cast from the silicone

56
00:03:57,240 --> 00:04:00,400
and sculpt a one-eyed
yokai face over it with clay.

57
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:02,740
Then take a mold with plaster

58
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:05,060
and throw away the clay inside
once it's no longer needed.

59
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:09,800
Next, whip the latex foam well
until it's smooth and even.

60
00:04:10,540 --> 00:04:14,400
Once you've thoroughly poured the
latex foam into the mold you just made,

61
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:16,680
bake it slowly in the oven.

62
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:19,020
Feels like we're making a cake or something.

63
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:21,160
Open the mold and it's done!

64
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:24,800
All that's left is to glue it together and paint it,
and we're finished.

65
00:04:25,260 --> 00:04:28,240
It's easy,
so please try making one yourselves!

66
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:29,900
The end.

67
00:04:31,340 --> 00:04:33,060
That turned out pretty realistic.

68
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:36,000
Alright,
let's try scaring the Chief with it.

69
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,400
Aaaaaaah!

70
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:44,500
I'm home!

71
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:53,840
Who are you?

72
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:56,940
Aaaaaaah!

73
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:58,500
Aaaaaaah!

74
00:04:58,500 --> 00:04:59,680
Aaaaaaah!

75
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:08,180
Stop it, it's me!

76
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:10,560
It's your dear subordinate, Ryotsu!

77
00:05:10,860 --> 00:05:11,580
I won't be fooled!

78
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:14,700
Chief, that really is Ryo-chan!

79
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:17,140
Reiko made the special makeup!

80
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:18,540
I can't believe that!

81
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:19,400
It's really true!

82
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:21,420
Just watch.

83
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:23,760
There, over there!

84
00:05:24,380 --> 00:05:26,000
It's just a five-yen coin.

85
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,100
Well, I'll take it anyway.

86
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:29,580
No doubt about it, it's Joe.

87
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:32,080
I keep telling you, it's me!

88
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:33,760
My head's spinning.

89
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:35,700
What's the meaning of this?

90
00:05:36,060 --> 00:05:38,480
Aren't you going to be in
tonight's ghost contest?

91
00:05:38,900 --> 00:05:40,840
Even I don't really want to do it.

92
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:42,660
I'm forcing myself to dress like this,
you know.

93
00:05:42,660 --> 00:05:44,700
Don't get your face so close.

94
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:45,780
How creepy.

95
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:47,820
Senpai, we need to head to the venue soon.

96
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:49,260
Is it that late already?

97
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:50,820
You're going dressed like that?

98
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:53,060
I'll drive you there.

99
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:54,200
Do that.

100
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:56,200
I can't stand it if this
turns into a big commotion.

101
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:58,920
Terai! Hey, Terai, are you all right?

102
00:06:02,580 --> 00:06:04,340
You came to, Terai?

103
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:09,300
Aaaah! Yō-chan, you hurry up and get going.

104
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:11,120
Eeeeeh!

105
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:19,320
Aaaah! Look, look at that!

106
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:24,640
It's Mr. Nakada's Ferrari, seriously!
Total jackpot vibes.

107
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:29,400
Should we invite him to go for a drive together?
Let's do it.

108
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:43,800
Don't make it 1,325 yen.

109
00:06:51,020 --> 00:06:51,820
Sake.

110
00:06:58,260 --> 00:07:00,840
Senpai, please stop fooling around.

111
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:03,520
They're the ones who called out to us,
so I just answered, that's all.

112
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:06,240
I'll go check. Please wait a moment.

113
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:08,820
Yeah, ugh, I want to sleep until we arrive.

114
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:16,900
Sorry!

115
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,880
I never thought we'd actually get a Ferrari.

116
00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:25,880
This one would sell for a lot.

117
00:07:29,180 --> 00:07:31,940
Was that a groan?
Maybe I'm imagining things.

118
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:36,560
The driving has gotten rough somehow.

119
00:07:44,140 --> 00:07:45,820
You idiot!

120
00:07:45,820 --> 00:07:52,740
You idiot!

121
00:07:52,740 --> 00:07:53,580
What was that?

122
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:55,740
I just saw something weird!

123
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:57,180
Ow

124
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:57,660
What?

125
00:07:57,660 --> 00:07:58,000
What is it?

126
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:04,080
Who the hell are you?

127
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:07,800
What?

128
00:08:08,820 --> 00:08:11,860
I bet you're the new car thief in town

129
00:08:11,860 --> 00:08:13,960
Look! A car thief!

130
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:15,600
You're not getting away!

131
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:16,520
Nooo!

132
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:17,380
Here it comes!

133
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:18,480
Look!

134
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:23,080
Wan tan shi in ja han sa chicchi

135
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:24,800
Help!

136
00:08:27,660 --> 00:08:28,580
Help me, officer!

137
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:29,980
I got it out.

138
00:08:35,780 --> 00:08:36,880
It's out!

139
00:08:37,640 --> 00:08:38,820
Don't leave me behind anymore!

140
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:44,920
Damn it, he stole my credit.

141
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:49,700
Whoops, I have to hurry.
The ghost contest is about to start.

142
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:51,740
It closed.

143
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:53,120
Hey, it's gonna go off!

144
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:55,380
Made it in time.

145
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:00,120
Let me see, did I have any loose change?

146
00:09:01,660 --> 00:09:02,700
What's that?

147
00:09:15,340 --> 00:09:18,540
What? Like he'd run into
a ghost or something.

148
00:09:18,540 --> 00:09:22,160
Right. I was wearing that
super-realistic ghost makeup.

149
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:26,180
If I cause a ruckus in town again,
the Chief will chew me out.

150
00:09:28,660 --> 00:09:31,280
Come on, come on, it won't come off!

151
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:40,940
There he is, that's him!

152
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:42,580
Oh crap, we're in trouble!

153
00:09:49,340 --> 00:09:52,040
Damn it, if I get caught,
they'll find out it's me!

154
00:09:59,380 --> 00:10:00,220
Aaaaaaah

155
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:01,360
me

156
00:10:17,940 --> 00:10:20,760
You can't escape from this place!

157
00:10:21,180 --> 00:10:22,460
Get down here now!

158
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:29,280
That ghost right there!

159
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:32,080
Stop resisting and come down!

160
00:10:37,260 --> 00:10:38,720
Hey, how about it?

161
00:10:50,060 --> 00:10:51,860
I got away somehow, but...

162
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:55,140
So, what do I do now?

163
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:01,980
A taxi, I guess it can't be helped.

164
00:11:01,980 --> 00:11:03,340
Double or nothing, let's try getting in.

165
00:11:09,280 --> 00:11:12,040
Mr. Driver, please don't be surprised.

166
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:13,400
What is it?

167
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:14,200
See?

168
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:16,580
But if you look closely,
you can tell it's just makeup.

169
00:11:16,580 --> 00:11:18,620
Everyone's freaking out,
it's such a problem.

170
00:11:18,620 --> 00:11:20,860
Phew, I'm saved. What a good driver.

171
00:11:20,860 --> 00:11:21,980
Good, good.

172
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:23,860
Where to?

173
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:25,480
To Manpuku Temple, please.

174
00:11:45,780 --> 00:11:47,120
I'm really late

175
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:50,180
It's awfully quiet here.

176
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:51,920
It's not already over, is it?

177
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:54,020
What's with that taxi?

178
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:56,620
It took off before I even paid!

179
00:11:57,400 --> 00:11:58,040
Oh well.

180
00:11:58,500 --> 00:11:59,840
Got a little bit of a bonus.

181
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:05,100
It's so dark I can't see my feet.

182
00:12:09,220 --> 00:12:09,880
You guys are pretty considerate.

183
00:12:11,460 --> 00:12:14,000
Sorry, sorry for being late.

184
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,140
Who are you?

185
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,360
Is that the old lady from the candy shop?

186
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:20,140
With makeup that thick,
you can't even see properly, can you?

187
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:26,160
The angle of the hand is a bit off.

188
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:27,060
Something like this, I think.

189
00:12:48,480 --> 00:12:57,800
So that's why. You're a participant too Well,
well, everyone's makeup is amazing!

190
00:12:57,800 --> 00:13:05,100
It doesn't look like a shopping district ghost contest at all.
Alright, I'll hide over there, so let's give them a good scare.

191
00:13:06,380 --> 00:13:09,620
Yeah, I'll give them a real fright.
Just you wait and see!

192
00:13:10,580 --> 00:13:10,860
me

193
00:13:25,460 --> 00:13:27,140
Where did you go last night?

194
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:29,160
That's my line.

195
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:33,240
I was waiting at Manpuku-ji the whole time too,
you know.

196
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:35,600
But not a single customer showed up!

197
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:38,960
Manpuku-ji?

198
00:13:40,860 --> 00:13:43,500
It was Bunpuku-ji, not Manpuku-ji!

199
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:45,900
What?! No way!

200
00:13:46,420 --> 00:13:47,660
I'm not lying.

201
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:50,140
It's written right here, see?

202
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:52,620
It's true.

203
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:55,880
But I met the other people playing ghosts!

204
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:59,360
Manpuku-ji is that temple,
and there should be no one there now.

205
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:00,200
Huh!

206
00:14:00,700 --> 00:14:02,220
Then who did I meet?

207
00:14:02,620 --> 00:14:05,960
Don't tell me you're
saying you met real ghosts!

208
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:11,320
Now that I think about it, those guys were
too realistic for shopping street people!

209
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:12,220
No way.

210
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:15,560
Ghosts, in this age of advanced science?

211
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:17,120
Enough already, Ryotsu!

212
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:19,380
You were probably slacking
off somewhere and got late,

213
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:21,780
so that's a lame excuse to cover it up,
isn't it?

214
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:25,420
Come to think of it, there was a ghost
commotion last night, wasn't there?

215
00:14:25,420 --> 00:14:28,340
Surely it wasn't you who caused it?

216
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:30,540
N-no, it wasn't me, it wasn't me!

217
00:14:30,540 --> 00:14:33,280
But my story is true, I swear it.

218
00:14:34,260 --> 00:14:35,700
Are you still half asleep or something?

219
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:43,300
Ghosts don't exist, obviously. But if they really did,
I'd pay money just to see them.

220
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:49,920
If we use those ghosts, step right up!
Terror level: 120%!

221
00:14:49,920 --> 00:14:54,120
They're all real, and you can even shake hands with them.
Matsuda is still talked about to this day.

222
00:15:00,260 --> 00:15:02,720
And purikura booths where you
can take a two-shot with a ghost!

223
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:05,180
The Obakecchi, a ghost you can raise!

224
00:15:07,480 --> 00:15:09,680
And a place where you can play with ghosts.

225
00:15:10,580 --> 00:15:13,080
If we build a huge leisure land,

226
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:16,820
we'll be filthy rich for sure!

227
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:22,740
The Chief got in the way
and cost me all that profit,

228
00:15:22,740 --> 00:15:25,040
so I'll make it back a thousandfold!

229
00:15:31,260 --> 00:15:33,900
Aaaaah! Now!

230
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:36,960
It's fine.

231
00:15:40,380 --> 00:15:41,140
A ghost!

232
00:15:41,140 --> 00:15:43,500
You're the ghost, you know!

233
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:45,220
Don't be scared of my face!

234
00:15:45,220 --> 00:15:46,600
It's me, it's me!

235
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:48,060
The one-eyed yokai from yesterday, remember?

236
00:15:48,060 --> 00:15:49,300
But...

237
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:51,360
Yesterday's was just special makeup!

238
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:52,500
See, it's me.

239
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:55,480
Hey, is everyone here?

240
00:15:55,940 --> 00:15:57,140
Come on out!

241
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:00,160
What?

242
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:02,940
So you were human all along?

243
00:16:02,940 --> 00:16:04,040
Yes!

244
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:06,520
And I thought you were one of us.

245
00:16:07,280 --> 00:16:08,380
Don't be ridiculous.

246
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:16,220
You're moping around. If you've got time to spare for ghost contests, why not go out into town and get people moving instead?
That's a good idea, isn't it?

247
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:25,660
But these days, no matter where you go, even at night, it's bright everywhere.
Those people glued to their cell phones and games don't even notice you standing right behind them.

248
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:31,300
There's just too much stimulation. Honestly,
at this rate, business is going to dry up for us.

249
00:16:34,900 --> 00:16:38,575
How pathetic. The world's come to an end.
Are you even ghosts?

250
00:16:38,625 --> 00:16:42,780
Listen, ghosts are only worth something
if people are scared of them, right?

251
00:16:45,580 --> 00:16:51,560
Alright! From now on I'll train you so you're not embarrassed to be ghosts!
Understood?

252
00:16:51,980 --> 00:16:52,680
But...

253
00:16:53,060 --> 00:16:54,000
Got a problem with that?

254
00:16:54,340 --> 00:16:55,080
No, sir.

255
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:56,300
Good.

256
00:16:57,680 --> 00:16:59,220
I'm getting dizzy.

257
00:16:59,220 --> 00:17:00,892
Ah ah, I'm getting dizzy too,

258
00:17:00,942 --> 00:17:17,760
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuugh...

259
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:19,060
Not scary at all!

260
00:17:19,420 --> 00:17:20,800
There's no way I can do that!

261
00:17:28,860 --> 00:17:33,440
What? There's no way an arrow
like that hits the target!

262
00:17:37,840 --> 00:17:40,680
Hey! Break it again and I'll
use the dish on your head!

263
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:41,160
Aaaaaah!

264
00:17:46,420 --> 00:17:48,820
Are you making fun of me? I can't dance!

265
00:18:04,020 --> 00:18:23,520
Nngggghhhh...

266
00:18:33,820 --> 00:18:35,120
I'm exhausted.

267
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:37,580
I didn't realize I could be this strict.

268
00:18:37,580 --> 00:18:39,680
Alright, next, 500 bunny hops!

269
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:42,680
I can't do it anymore!

270
00:18:42,680 --> 00:18:44,520
Shut up, do it louder!

271
00:18:44,520 --> 00:18:51,020
So we finally open tomorrow night

272
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:53,380
Becoming a millionaire
is right within reach!

273
00:18:54,160 --> 00:18:55,140
Ryo-chan

274
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:56,600
Ryo-chan

275
00:18:58,620 --> 00:18:59,340
What's wrong with you?

276
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:01,840
Why are you so pale?

277
00:19:01,840 --> 00:19:03,580
Are you feeling sick or something?

278
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:04,880
I see.

279
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:07,460
Nothing's wrong with my body, though.

280
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:08,500
Is that so?

281
00:19:08,860 --> 00:19:10,380
You look really worn out.

282
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:11,360
And look,

283
00:19:11,360 --> 00:19:13,300
you've left more than
half your katsudon uneaten!

284
00:19:14,060 --> 00:19:16,120
Normally, Ryo-chan would eat katsudon plus

285
00:19:16,120 --> 00:19:18,120
ramen and even yakisoba on top of that!

286
00:19:18,120 --> 00:19:20,500
Sometimes you even order tempura
bowls with a side of cold soba!

287
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:24,140
I just don't have much of an appetite,
that's all.

288
00:19:24,700 --> 00:19:26,660
It's just that it's been hot every day.

289
00:19:27,580 --> 00:19:29,600
I think we should consult the Chief.

290
00:19:30,120 --> 00:19:30,480
Yes, we should.

291
00:19:39,580 --> 00:19:44,240
He went out after all.

292
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:46,600
Yeah, let's follow him.

293
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:51,780
Listen up, tomorrow is finally opening day.

294
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:54,940
I'm going to see the
results of your training.

295
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:58,560
And since today is the last training session,
it'll be especially harsh.

296
00:20:00,160 --> 00:20:01,900
He's a real ghost, you know.

297
00:20:01,900 --> 00:20:04,640
So what Ryo-chan said was true after all.

298
00:20:05,060 --> 00:20:07,360
The senior officer is possessed by a ghost.

299
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:09,400
At this rate, he might be killed by it.

300
00:20:09,400 --> 00:20:11,140
Chief, what should we do?

301
00:20:21,300 --> 00:20:22,920
Why on earth would I have to face ghosts

302
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:26,600
Yes, that face of yours
already shows grim resolve.

303
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:27,200
Grim

304
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:29,600
If you go out to meet the ghosts tonight,

305
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:31,800
you're sure to be killed by them.

306
00:20:32,120 --> 00:20:35,260
Uh-oh, if my plan gets found out here,
everything's ruined.

307
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:38,660
What? You can't trust
a word this guy says...

308
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:39,900
Idiot!

309
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:44,560
Our Gachondera family has had proper
exorcism methods for generations!

310
00:20:44,560 --> 00:20:46,580
That's right! Listen to me, Ryotsu!

311
00:20:46,940 --> 00:20:48,380
It's for your own good!

312
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:52,560
No, even if you hate it,
I can't just abandon you like this!

313
00:20:52,780 --> 00:20:55,940
As your superior,
as a man, I will protect you!

314
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:58,240
No! Today is an important day!

315
00:20:58,540 --> 00:21:00,260
I have to go no matter what!

316
00:21:00,400 --> 00:21:02,320
Everyone, hurry up and hold him down!

317
00:21:02,820 --> 00:21:04,040
Hurry, hold him down!

318
00:21:04,800 --> 00:21:06,000
What are you doing!

319
00:21:08,120 --> 00:21:11,700
You pervert! You lecherous priest! What do you think you're doing,
stripping a man naked!

320
00:21:11,700 --> 00:21:12,080
Gaah!

321
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:14,980
I'm writing a charm to ward off evil.

322
00:21:14,980 --> 00:21:16,740
This is humiliating, stop it!

323
00:21:17,140 --> 00:21:17,800
No!

324
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:18,840
Be quiet.

325
00:21:18,840 --> 00:21:21,840
I can't write good characters
unless I concentrate.

326
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:26,220
Don't look up the characters!

327
00:21:27,220 --> 00:21:29,800
What's with the "houren"? Gashon gashon

328
00:21:29,800 --> 00:21:31,800
Nanman dabu, nanman dabu

329
00:21:31,800 --> 00:21:33,620
Gashon gashon

330
00:21:33,620 --> 00:21:36,840
Eroi muesutamu, gashon gashon

331
00:21:36,840 --> 00:21:40,140
Kanji great study, gashon gashon

332
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:45,100
Shiroku te ku ga chon ga chon

333
00:21:45,100 --> 00:21:47,800
Begone, evil spirits! Begone, evil spirits!

334
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:50,580
Drive them away, drive them away!

335
00:21:50,580 --> 00:21:52,580
Purify him!

336
00:21:53,780 --> 00:21:57,360
Gachon gachon no hara horo hire hare

337
00:21:57,360 --> 00:21:59,260
Jan wa chon wa no kue kue

338
00:21:59,260 --> 00:22:01,180
And while we're at it,

339
00:22:01,180 --> 00:22:03,580
Shee! Shee! Shee! Shee!

340
00:22:07,080 --> 00:22:09,360
Begone, evil spirits! Begone, evil spirits!

341
00:22:09,360 --> 00:22:12,740
In the name of the moon, I'll punish you!

342
00:22:13,740 --> 00:22:16,220
Hang in there, Ryotsu! Endure it!

343
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:19,440
Afuremotae-san, Afuremotae-san

344
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:22,180
In the name of the moon, I'll punish you!

345
00:22:22,180 --> 00:22:25,400
Gachon gachon no kuekue

346
00:22:25,400 --> 00:22:29,340
Shaiyā shaiyā chon wa no kuekue

347
00:22:30,020 --> 00:22:33,040
Gachon gachon no kuekue

348
00:22:33,040 --> 00:22:33,880
It's coming out!

349
00:22:35,500 --> 00:22:36,940
Gachon!

350
00:22:36,940 --> 00:22:38,500
Gachon gachon

351
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:40,620
Begone, evil spirits!

352
00:22:40,620 --> 00:22:43,260
Begone, evil spirits!

353
00:22:43,260 --> 00:22:46,320
Gachon gachon

354
00:22:46,320 --> 00:22:47,420
How can I be dealing with this!

355
00:22:47,420 --> 00:22:50,060
I borrowed every last
yen for this haunted house!

356
00:22:57,080 --> 00:22:58,300
No, senpai.

357
00:22:58,920 --> 00:23:00,640
No, senpai.

358
00:23:00,640 --> 00:23:01,600
Wait, senpai.

359
00:23:02,700 --> 00:23:05,560
You guys came to pick me up?

360
00:23:06,940 --> 00:23:07,680
Alright.

361
00:23:08,660 --> 00:23:09,440
Senpai.

362
00:23:09,440 --> 00:23:09,920
Ryotsu.

363
00:23:09,920 --> 00:23:11,480
Ryo-chan, come back.

364
00:23:11,480 --> 00:23:14,000
Alright, straight to the venue, quick!

365
00:23:16,020 --> 00:23:17,160
Please help us.

366
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:18,720
This guy's scary.

367
00:23:19,780 --> 00:23:20,180
What?

368
00:23:20,880 --> 00:23:22,960
What is this? What's going on, you guys?

369
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:25,700
You're not seriously scared of a little chant like this,
are you?

370
00:23:25,700 --> 00:23:30,600
We came here to turn down this job.

371
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:33,940
We understand you're trying your hardest, Ryo-san,
but

372
00:23:33,940 --> 00:23:35,340
we just can't keep up with you.

373
00:23:36,940 --> 00:23:37,560
Even if it's tough,

374
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:40,980
So you're the ones who
were possessing Ryotsu?

375
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:44,760
No, he was the one possessing us.

376
00:23:44,760 --> 00:23:47,500
He's the true king of money.

377
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:52,080
What?! What about the 1,225,000 yen I poured into this?
Who's going to make that up to me?

378
00:23:52,520 --> 00:23:54,180
There's no way I'm quitting now!

379
00:23:56,680 --> 00:23:58,300
Wait! My money source!

380
00:23:58,920 --> 00:23:59,720
Ryotsu!

381
00:24:04,420 --> 00:24:07,060
Incredibly, the woman I picked up late
at night on the Metropolitan Expressway

382
00:24:07,060 --> 00:24:09,200
driving a Corvette was
a super-beautiful driver,

383
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:10,820
and she turned out to be Maria's mom!

384
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:14,240
So that means she's that
bookshelf old man's wife?

385
00:24:14,600 --> 00:24:17,760
Even if the ward office approves,
this Ryotsu Kankichi won't allow it!

386
00:24:17,760 --> 00:24:20,500
Next time:
the beautiful wife gets super intense.

387
00:24:20,980 --> 00:24:21,620
See you then.

388
00:24:30,440 --> 00:24:37,060
People gossip that I'm a
woman who can't fall in love,

389
00:24:37,060 --> 00:24:42,940
but I have mountains of things I want to do.

390
00:24:44,720 --> 00:24:52,020
I want to ride a motorbike
across the vast desert.

391
00:24:52,020 --> 00:24:59,180
I want to be freer than a bird.

392
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:07,200
A lady's dreams change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

393
00:25:08,820 --> 00:25:15,320
My heart in love, sorry, please wait for me.

394
00:25:15,320 --> 00:25:22,220
Future like a panorama,
the dazzle will come soon enough.

395
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:26,493
You understand, right?

396
00:25:26,543 --> 00:25:30,080
Sorry, please wait for me.

